# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
import json, io

data = {
 "pdf_page": 469,
 "book_page": 439,
 "verified_by": "claude-opus-5",
 "verified_on": "2026-09-13",
 "entries": [
  {
   "entry": 0,
   "root": "Sphallein",
   "verdict": "disputed",
   "modern_form": "Ancient Greek σφάλλω (sphállō) 'to trip up, make fall, baffle', from PIE *(s)gʷʰh₂el- 'to stumble' (cf. Sanskrit skhalate, Armenian sxalem); NOT of Semitic origin",
   "note": "The Greek word and the gloss are right: σφάλλω 'to cause to fall, trip up, make slip' is well attested from Homer on, and the citation form σφάλλειν is its infinitive. What is wrong is the origin note. Nourai's 'From an unknown Semitic root' is Klein's remark about the DERIVATIVE ἄσφαλτος, not about σφάλλω: Klein p.114 s.v. asphalt writes 'Gk. ἄσφαλτος, which is of uncertain, possibly Sem., origin' and refers to H. Lewy, Die semitischen Fremdwörter im Griechischen (1895) p.53. σφάλλω itself has a solid Indo-European etymology — Beekes (EDG 2010, via Wiktionary) derives it from PIE *(s)gʷʰh₂el- 'to stumble', with Sanskrit स्खलति (skhalati) 'stumbles' and Old Armenian սխալեմ (sxalem) 'to err' as cognates. (Pokorny 985-987 instead put σφάλλω under (s)p(h)el- 'split', which is the root of the second chart on this page — an older view now abandoned.) So the root box mixes a real Greek verb with a Semitic-origin claim that belongs to a different word and that no modern authority applies to σφάλλω.",
   "note_fa": "سرواژهٔ این نمودار، فعل یونانی σφάλλω (مصدر sphallein) «لغزاندن، بر زمین زدن» است که واژه و معنای آن درست ثبت شده؛ اما یادداشت «از ریشه‌ای سامی ناشناخته» نادرست جای گرفته است. کلاین (ص ۱۱۴) این نکته را نه دربارهٔ sphallein بلکه دربارهٔ مشتق آن ἄσφαλτος می‌گوید («خاستگاهش نامعلوم و شاید سامی است»، با ارجاع به لِوی ۱۸۹۵ ص ۵۳). خودِ sphallein ریشه‌شناسی هندواروپایی روشنی دارد: بیکس آن را از *(s)gʷʰh₂el- «لغزیدن، سکندری خوردن» می‌داند، هم‌ریشه با skhalati سنسکریت و sxalem ارمنی. پوکورنی (ص ۹۸۵) آن را زیر ریشهٔ (s)p(h)el- «شکافتن» آورده بود که دیدگاهی کهنه است. پس: ادعای سامی‌بودن را پژوهش امروزی رد می‌کند، هرچند واژه و معنای یونانی درست است.",
   "sources": [
    "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%CF%83%CF%86%CE%AC%CE%BB%CE%BB%CF%89",
    "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E1%BC%84%CF%83%CF%86%CE%B1%CE%BB%CF%84%CE%BF%CF%82",
    "https://www.ahdictionary.com/word/search.html?q=asphalt"
   ],
   "ref_check": [
    {"ref": "KLN:114", "status": "partial", "note": "Klein 1966 p.114 (page marker '114' at line 3646 of KLN_1966.txt) s.v. asphalt: 'F. asphalte, fr. Late L. asphaltus, fr. Gk. ἄσφαλτος, which is of uncertain, possibly Sem., origin. See Heinrich Lewy, Die semitischen Fremdwörter im Griechischen, Berlin, 1895, p.53.' The page is exactly right, but Klein's 'possibly Semitic' is said of ἄσφαλτος; he says nothing about σφάλλειν, and he does not analyse asphaltos as a- + sphallein."},
    {"ref": "AHD:78", "status": "partial", "note": "The 1975 AHD New College Edition p.78 is not on disk (only Watkins's IE-root appendix is, and grep -i 'sphal|asphalt' in AHD_watkins1985.txt returns no root entry). The current online AHD s.v. asphalt prints only '[Middle English aspalt, from Medieval Latin asphaltus, from Greek asphaltos.]' — no Semitic source and no a- + sphallein decomposition."}
   ],
   "consulted": [
    {"src": "POK", "where": "IEW 985-987, (s)p(h)el-1 (POK_full.txt line 79838 ff.)", "stance": "contradicts", "note": "Pokorny files σφάλλω under the IE root (s)p(h)el- 'spalten': 'zu σφαλάσσειν also σφαλός … und σφάλλω \"throw (originally with Prügeln), toss, fling\" … from which \"bring to collapse, injure, deceive\"'. An Indo-European etymology, not a Semitic one — though this particular assignment is itself now superseded."},
    {"src": "AHD", "where": "Watkins 1985, appendix of IE roots", "stance": "silent", "note": "No root *sphal- / *(s)gʷʰel- in the appendix and no ASPHALT among the English reflexes listed under spel-1 'to split, break off' (grep of AHD_watkins1985.txt)."},
    {"src": "KLN", "where": "Klein 1966 p.114 s.v. asphalt", "stance": "partial", "note": "'Gk. ἄσφαλτος, which is of uncertain, possibly Sem., origin' — the only source behind Nourai's 'unknown Semitic root', and it concerns asphaltos, not sphallein."},
    {"src": "IEC", "where": "Mann, col. s.v. sphált- (IEC.txt line 17002)", "stance": "partial", "note": "'sphált- \"bang, burst\". WP II, 677. Skt. sphaṭāmi … Gk. sphalássō, v. \"cut, stab\"' — Mann too has a Greek sphal- family, but under 'burst/split', i.e. the second root on this page, not a Semitic source."}
   ],
   "nodes": [
    {
     "id": 1,
     "lang": "Greek",
     "words": "a-sphallein; asphaltos",
